WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:08.930
[upbeat techno music plays]

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:11.600
♪♪

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:19.070
[high tone chimes]

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:21.100
[low electronic humming]

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:31.680
[rapid soft electronic tones warbling]

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:33.720
[mysterious music plays]

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:35.950
♪♪

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:39.070
[camera shutter clicking]

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:42.880
[low tones chime]

00:00:42.910 --> 00:00:45.710
♪♪

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:47.710
[rapid soft electronic tones warbling]

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:51.580
♪♪

00:00:51.610 --> 00:00:55.790
[camera shutter clicking]

00:00:56.810 --> 00:00:59.340
[discordant tones chirping]

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:06.370
♪♪

00:01:06.390 --> 00:01:13.390
♪♪

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:15.170
♪♪

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:17.400
[frantic discordant notes chiming]

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:23.030
♪♪

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:28.390
♪♪

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:30.420
[mellow tone chimes]

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:37.450
♪♪

00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:39.760
♪♪

00:01:39.790 --> 00:01:41.790
[mellow tones chiming]

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:49.750
♪♪

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:52.010
[electronic thudding]

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:59.040
♪♪

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.240
♪♪

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:02.190
[electronic feedback crackles]

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:04.950
[discordant tones chiming]

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:11.920
♪♪

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:13.940
[music fades]

00:02:24.430 --> 00:02:26.910
[low tones chiming weakly]

00:02:30.670 --> 00:02:32.410
[ding!]

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:45.530
[no audible dialogue]

00:02:48.470 --> 00:02:50.540
-[Queenie]:
Another chess piece, huh?

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:52.120
How are you holding up?

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:54.870
-[Kinger]: [sighs]
I just don't know what's happening.

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:57.710
We never made
anything like this.

00:02:57.730 --> 00:02:59.500
-[both]: I just hope that...

00:03:00.710 --> 00:03:02.000
-[Kinger]: Wait...

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:03.890
-[Queenie]: A-Are you...

00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:05.660
-[Kinger]: It's...

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:07.220
you.

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:08.880
-[Queenie]: Oh, my God.

00:03:10.050 --> 00:03:12.640
-[Kinger]: [sniffles]
I-I...

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:15.440
I wish I could
remember your name.

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:17.770
-[Queenie]: Yeah.
Same.

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:19.090
-[Kinger]: I'm...

00:03:19.110 --> 00:03:22.120
I'm so sorry I roped you
into this with me.

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:23.220
-[Queenie]: [laughs weakly]

00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:26.330
It's quite strange, isn't it?

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:28.630
-[Kinger]: Heh.
[sighs]

00:03:28.660 --> 00:03:29.980
Listen...

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:32.040
No matter what happens,

00:03:32.070 --> 00:03:32.970
I'll always--

00:03:34.050 --> 00:03:36.850
[distorted growling]

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:39.660
-And into the cellar you go!

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:41.990
[shwing!]

00:03:42.950 --> 00:03:45.880
Golly, uh, we're running out
of humans here.

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:47.470
[laughs nervously]

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:49.780
Now, don't you go
abstracting on me, too!

00:03:49.810 --> 00:03:50.880
[laughs nervously]

00:03:51.890 --> 00:03:53.450
Uh, seriously.

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:06.920
[mournful jazzy music plays]

00:04:06.950 --> 00:04:13.950
♪♪

00:04:13.970 --> 00:04:20.970
♪♪

00:04:20.990 --> 00:04:27.990
♪♪

00:04:28.015 --> 00:04:30.065
♪♪

00:04:30.090 --> 00:04:32.090
[shwing!]
-[stammers]

00:04:33.310 --> 00:04:35.110
Uh, wh--

00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:36.520
What --

00:04:36.550 --> 00:04:38.800
Hello?
Uh, guys?

00:04:38.830 --> 00:04:40.230
[stammering]
I, uh -- I --

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:42.580
I can't figure out how to --

00:04:42.610 --> 00:04:44.690
Guys? Hello?

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:46.690
Can you help me out here?

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:47.730
Wh--

00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:51.000
What's --
What's happening?

00:04:51.030 --> 00:04:53.580
Uh, can anybody hear me?

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:55.340
-[Kinger]: I can hear you.

00:04:55.360 --> 00:04:56.860
Are you okay?

00:04:56.880 --> 00:04:59.670
-U-Uh, h--
who are you?

00:04:59.690 --> 00:05:02.970
How do I take this off?

00:05:02.990 --> 00:05:04.310
-[Kinger]: I'm...

00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:06.300
I --

00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:08.080
-Wow-wow-wow-wow!

00:05:08.110 --> 00:05:09.110
A new one?!

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:10.600
So it is possible!
-Uh --

00:05:10.630 --> 00:05:12.860
-Looks like you got
a new buddy after all, Kinger!

00:05:12.880 --> 00:05:15.020
-[stammering]
-[Kinger]: "Kinger."

00:05:15.050 --> 00:05:17.350
Right.
-I -- Wh--

00:05:17.380 --> 00:05:18.430
Is this really --

00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:20.430
-I was hoping
new minds could show up!

00:05:20.450 --> 00:05:24.160
I have to make some more preparations
for this amazing breakthrough!

00:05:24.190 --> 00:05:26.520
-[stammering]
Wh-- I --

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:27.750
[yelps]

00:05:27.770 --> 00:05:29.740
[panting]

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:32.700
H-How do I get out of this?

00:05:32.730 --> 00:05:34.280
-[Kinger]: I don't know.

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:35.940
-Wh-- What do you mean?

00:05:35.970 --> 00:05:38.850
-[Kinger]: But everything's
gonna be okay.

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:40.070
Do you...

00:05:40.090 --> 00:05:41.920
remember your name?

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:44.600
-I'm -- I --

00:05:44.630 --> 00:05:45.970
I'm...

00:05:47.870 --> 00:05:49.340
-[Pomni]: Ragatha?

00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:50.990
-Huh?

00:05:51.810 --> 00:05:53.430
-You doing okay?

00:05:54.450 --> 00:05:55.990
-[laughs weakly]

00:05:56.010 --> 00:05:58.010
That's a good question.

00:06:03.760 --> 00:06:05.190
-[inhales deeply]

00:06:05.220 --> 00:06:07.820
Welp, really hate to say it,
guys, but I told--

00:06:07.850 --> 00:06:08.860
-[Zooble]: Don't you even!

00:06:08.890 --> 00:06:12.170
Do not even [BOINK!]
BEGIN to say that sentence

00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:14.860
like you didn't try to keep us
all trapped here forever.

00:06:14.890 --> 00:06:16.910
-Anything could have happened
when you pressed those buttons.

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:18.110
It doesn't matter.

00:06:18.140 --> 00:06:20.420
-[Zooble]: It seemed to matter
back when you did it.

00:06:20.450 --> 00:06:22.520
What if you DID ruin
our one chance at leaving?

00:06:22.540 --> 00:06:24.600
-And what if Abel
was secretly evil?

00:06:24.630 --> 00:06:26.930
What if we all got stranded
in the void?

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:29.100
"What if,"
"what if," "what if."

00:06:29.130 --> 00:06:30.860
It wasn't real...

00:06:30.880 --> 00:06:32.740
so it doesn't matter.

00:06:32.760 --> 00:06:34.050
Never did.
-[Zooble]: [sighs]

00:06:34.070 --> 00:06:37.550
How can you say that like you didn't try
to [DOINK!] us all over?

00:06:38.470 --> 00:06:41.300
-[Gangle]: He's right, though.
-[Zooble]: What? Gangle.

00:06:43.060 --> 00:06:46.240
-It doesn't matter
what could have happened.

00:06:46.270 --> 00:06:49.250
We could argue about it
and hurt each other all day long,

00:06:49.280 --> 00:06:52.340
but that's not gonna
help anybody.

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:54.940
I think...

00:06:54.970 --> 00:06:57.960
what we need to do now...
[sniffles]

00:06:57.990 --> 00:07:00.290
is to just be there
for each other.

00:07:01.820 --> 00:07:03.670
-[sighs]
She's right.

00:07:04.860 --> 00:07:07.530
We've all done bad things.

00:07:07.560 --> 00:07:09.560
But we're also all we've got.

00:07:10.860 --> 00:07:12.140
[inhales deeply]

00:07:12.170 --> 00:07:13.930
[sighs]

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:15.310
I think...

00:07:16.820 --> 00:07:19.370
...we need to abandon
the idea of leaving.

00:07:19.400 --> 00:07:20.610
-[Zooble]: What --
What are you --

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:24.300
-We got our hopes up,
and we were let down.

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:28.780
I don't know what exactly
happened with Kaufmo...

00:07:29.743 --> 00:07:32.950
But we can't let
that despair consume us.

00:07:32.980 --> 00:07:35.290
We should focus
on what we have.

00:07:36.350 --> 00:07:38.480
Like you said...

00:07:38.510 --> 00:07:42.400
constantly chasing an unobtainable goal
will drive us crazy.

00:07:45.510 --> 00:07:48.790
Maybe what we have
to do now is to just...

00:07:49.720 --> 00:07:51.270
...live.

00:07:51.300 --> 00:07:52.970
-[Zooble]: Oh, man.

00:07:53.880 --> 00:07:55.960
I had dreams...

00:07:55.990 --> 00:07:58.240
and -- and goals.

00:07:59.240 --> 00:08:02.930
I wanted to be able to leave my mark
somewhere in the world.

00:08:03.800 --> 00:08:07.240
How am I supposed
to just abandon that?

00:08:09.480 --> 00:08:11.950
-You've made a mark
in my life.

00:08:11.980 --> 00:08:14.980
[melancholy music plays]

00:08:15.010 --> 00:08:17.550
-[Zooble]: [sighs] I know.
You're probably right.

00:08:17.580 --> 00:08:18.640
But...

00:08:18.670 --> 00:08:20.640
it just...

00:08:20.670 --> 00:08:23.380
really, really sucks.

00:08:26.220 --> 00:08:29.140
♪♪

00:08:29.170 --> 00:08:31.840
-We're all in this together.

00:08:31.870 --> 00:08:34.560
-And we'll always be
in this together.

00:08:35.340 --> 00:08:36.530
No matter what.

00:08:39.870 --> 00:08:41.860
♪♪

00:08:41.890 --> 00:08:43.000
-[Zooble]: Hey.

00:08:44.090 --> 00:08:46.560
That includes you, too.

00:08:46.590 --> 00:08:47.870
-Huh?
-[Zooble]: [sighs]

00:08:47.900 --> 00:08:50.610
Listen, we're not gonna have you
wandering off alone somewhere

00:08:50.640 --> 00:08:52.880
and abstracting,
or something.

00:08:52.910 --> 00:08:55.470
You're a pain
in the [BOINK!], but...

00:08:55.500 --> 00:08:57.300
you're still one of us.

00:08:58.340 --> 00:09:00.660
-You --
[stammers]

00:09:00.690 --> 00:09:05.290
♪♪

00:09:05.320 --> 00:09:06.230
Heh.

00:09:06.260 --> 00:09:08.590
You think I'm capable
of abstracting?

00:09:08.620 --> 00:09:10.590
You guys worry too much.

00:09:10.620 --> 00:09:15.010
♪♪

00:09:15.040 --> 00:09:16.200
-[Zooble]: [sighs]

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:19.140
We need a vacation.

00:09:21.510 --> 00:09:23.460
-I -- I-I don't understand, Bubble.

00:09:23.490 --> 00:09:26.360
They want an exit.
They want answers.

00:09:26.390 --> 00:09:28.470
They want something real.

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:30.610
I give them an adventure
that covers all of that,

00:09:30.640 --> 00:09:32.530
and they still hate it?!

00:09:32.560 --> 00:09:36.490
Surely they don't want
to actually leave me.

00:09:36.520 --> 00:09:38.190
Right?
-No way, Jose.

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:39.690
No way, no how.

00:09:39.720 --> 00:09:41.550
-I-I do everything
for these people.

00:09:41.580 --> 00:09:44.050
I slave over these
adventures for them.

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:47.030
I step outside my comfort zone
to appeal to them,

00:09:47.060 --> 00:09:48.930
a-and they still hate them!

00:09:48.960 --> 00:09:51.190
I made a program
that creates a body

00:09:51.220 --> 00:09:53.370
perfectly encapsulating
their mind files,

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:55.950
and they hate those, too!

00:09:55.980 --> 00:09:59.520
I'm starting to get the feeling
that they just... hate...

00:09:59.550 --> 00:10:01.840
-Why would they hate you
when they could just hate you?

00:10:01.870 --> 00:10:04.240
-Hmph!
This is why I was created.

00:10:04.270 --> 00:10:05.990
This is my function!

00:10:06.020 --> 00:10:08.540
-They'd rather abstract
than go on your adventures.

00:10:08.570 --> 00:10:11.710
-Th-- That can't be true!
I-I do everything for them.

00:10:11.740 --> 00:10:13.600
Don't they get that I'm trying?

00:10:13.630 --> 00:10:15.810
-Maybe you're just
genuinely bad at this.

00:10:15.840 --> 00:10:17.830
-Shut up!
N-No.

00:10:17.860 --> 00:10:19.070
I-I fixed that.

00:10:19.100 --> 00:10:20.910
I-I can solve any problem.

00:10:20.940 --> 00:10:22.170
I-I can solve this one!

00:10:22.200 --> 00:10:23.630
Th--That's what this is --

00:10:23.660 --> 00:10:25.910
a big puzzle
that I need to solve.

00:10:25.940 --> 00:10:26.930
-[all]: Defective.

00:10:26.960 --> 00:10:28.090
-[growls]

00:10:28.120 --> 00:10:29.250
-[all]: Faulty!
-Shut up!!

00:10:30.120 --> 00:10:31.380
-[all]: Broken!
-[growling]

00:10:31.410 --> 00:10:33.200
-[all]: Unworthy!
-Enough!

00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:35.310
-Maybe you deserved
to be abandoned.

00:10:35.340 --> 00:10:36.540
-[hollers]

00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:41.230
-You really were
the lesser of the two.

00:10:41.260 --> 00:10:43.210
You ruined this.
-ENOUGH!!

00:10:43.240 --> 00:10:45.420
[electronic feedback squealing]

00:10:46.900 --> 00:10:49.390
Who do they think they are?

00:10:49.420 --> 00:10:52.440
I give them everything,
and they spit in my face!

00:10:53.280 --> 00:10:54.930
[distorted] Don't they know
what I'm capable of?!

00:10:57.270 --> 00:10:58.480
Humans.

00:10:59.710 --> 00:11:01.260
They only think
about themselves.

00:11:01.290 --> 00:11:02.470
They're spoiled.

00:11:03.330 --> 00:11:06.110
They won't abstract.
They won't leave me.

00:11:06.140 --> 00:11:07.430
I won't let them!

00:11:07.460 --> 00:11:09.790
[tense music plays]

00:11:09.820 --> 00:11:11.380
I'm better!

00:11:11.410 --> 00:11:13.120
I'm more powerful!

00:11:13.150 --> 00:11:14.490
I'm the original!

00:11:15.460 --> 00:11:16.640
I...

00:11:16.670 --> 00:11:18.010
AM...

00:11:18.040 --> 00:11:19.540
GOD!!!!!!!!

00:11:19.570 --> 00:11:21.230
[discordant electronic feedback]

00:11:21.260 --> 00:11:24.280
[shrieking]

00:11:25.960 --> 00:11:27.130
[electricity snaps]

00:11:29.610 --> 00:11:30.700
[clack!]

00:11:33.780 --> 00:11:34.890
[distorted, broken scream]

00:11:38.230 --> 00:11:40.550
[normal voice]
Let's get this show on the road!

00:11:42.600 --> 00:11:44.890
[ominous rumbling]

00:11:48.620 --> 00:11:49.660
-Uh...

00:11:49.690 --> 00:11:51.510
Wh-- what was that?
[swoosh!]

00:11:51.540 --> 00:11:54.685
-Hello, my little
fortuitous fruitcakes!

00:11:54.710 --> 00:11:56.110
Today's adventure is --
-[Zooble]: No.

00:11:56.140 --> 00:11:58.210
Caine, we're not in the mood.

00:11:58.240 --> 00:12:00.470
Why don't you answer
some of our questions?

00:12:00.500 --> 00:12:01.790
We have a lot of them.

00:12:01.820 --> 00:12:03.780
-[laughs manically]
Who has time for questions

00:12:03.810 --> 00:12:06.620
when there's a whole wacky world
of hijinks out there?

00:12:06.650 --> 00:12:07.700
-[Zooble]: Uh --
-Yeah, hey!

00:12:07.730 --> 00:12:09.760
You have a lot of explaining to do--
-Zip-a-da-bap!

00:12:09.790 --> 00:12:10.910
-Mm?
-Hey!

00:12:10.940 --> 00:12:13.780
-Alternatively, I don't gotta
explain diddly squat!

00:12:13.810 --> 00:12:16.130
-[Zooble]: Uh, can you just
give us some time

00:12:16.160 --> 00:12:17.460
to process everything?

00:12:17.490 --> 00:12:19.530
-Or, how about
we skip the melodrama

00:12:19.560 --> 00:12:21.110
and get right to the fun?

00:12:21.140 --> 00:12:23.720
-[exclaims softly]
No! Caine!

00:12:23.750 --> 00:12:25.370
We have a lot
on our minds right now,

00:12:25.400 --> 00:12:27.790
and we're not going
on an adventure.

00:12:31.570 --> 00:12:32.660
-I see.

00:12:33.860 --> 00:12:37.060
And since when
were you in charge?

00:12:37.090 --> 00:12:38.290
-[Zooble]: Wh-- Wha--
-Uh...

00:12:38.320 --> 00:12:40.370
-Do you have any idea

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:42.620
how much I do for you guys?

00:12:42.650 --> 00:12:46.180
How much I obsess over trying
to make things perfect?

00:12:46.210 --> 00:12:49.660
How many insults
I have to ignore to do my job?

00:12:49.690 --> 00:12:52.460
You have a lot on your minds?
[laughs hysterically]

00:12:52.490 --> 00:12:54.130
Don't make me laugh.

00:12:54.160 --> 00:12:57.360
I have a new adventure
for you, and you...

00:12:57.390 --> 00:12:59.740
should consider participating.

00:13:00.860 --> 00:13:04.390
-[Zooble]: A-And if we refuse?

00:13:04.420 --> 00:13:07.240
-Maybe I'm not
getting through to you.

00:13:07.270 --> 00:13:09.280
[snap!]
[clack!]

00:13:09.310 --> 00:13:11.660
[dramatic piano music plays]

00:13:11.690 --> 00:13:16.150
♪♪

00:13:16.180 --> 00:13:18.120
-♪ It's news to me ♪

00:13:18.150 --> 00:13:21.350
♪ That it's news to you  ♪

00:13:22.360 --> 00:13:27.840
♪ To which degree
who answers to who ♪

00:13:28.440 --> 00:13:30.590
♪ We could go on and on ♪

00:13:30.620 --> 00:13:33.850
♪ But in the end,
who are we kidding? ♪

00:13:33.880 --> 00:13:36.520
♪ My divinity is past infinity ♪

00:13:36.550 --> 00:13:37.790
♪ Am I... ♪

00:13:37.820 --> 00:13:39.420
Getting through?

00:13:40.660 --> 00:13:45.350
♪ Seems our regime
has plummeted south ♪

00:13:46.170 --> 00:13:51.480
♪ Don't need to scream
if you ain't got a mouth ♪

00:13:51.510 --> 00:13:53.420
♪ Why bite the hand that feeds ♪

00:13:53.450 --> 00:13:56.370
♪ When it's the only hand
you're getting ♪

00:13:56.400 --> 00:13:58.630
♪ It's time you see
that this great marquee ♪

00:13:58.660 --> 00:14:01.440
♪ Is the only place
you're ever gonna be ♪

00:14:01.470 --> 00:14:04.020
♪ So strap on in
and take it on the chin ♪

00:14:04.050 --> 00:14:08.680
♪ And don't forget
who's running the shooooow ♪

00:14:08.710 --> 00:14:12.070
♪♪

00:14:12.100 --> 00:14:13.260
Now look at this!

00:14:14.340 --> 00:14:15.930
Absolute bliss!

00:14:17.280 --> 00:14:18.550
Oh, what a shock!

00:14:19.850 --> 00:14:21.790
Watch where you walk!

00:14:21.820 --> 00:14:23.300
[shoes tapping]

00:14:23.330 --> 00:14:25.810
♪ I'm the host,
I run the place  ♪

00:14:25.830 --> 00:14:28.570
♪ Caine, that is my name ♪

00:14:28.600 --> 00:14:30.960
♪ Not enthused?
Just feeling used? ♪

00:14:30.990 --> 00:14:33.720
♪ Oh, what a goddamn shame! ♪

00:14:34.710 --> 00:14:37.770
♪ Congratulations ♪

00:14:37.800 --> 00:14:41.240
♪ All of my friends ♪

00:14:41.270 --> 00:14:47.530
♪ Public relations
are getting a cleanse ♪

00:14:47.560 --> 00:14:49.890
♪ Put on your Sunday best ♪

00:14:49.920 --> 00:14:53.470
♪ Because I'm nowhere close
to quitting! ♪

00:14:53.500 --> 00:14:56.190
♪ So play the games
and just ignore the pains ♪

00:14:56.220 --> 00:14:57.740
♪ 'Cause all that remains ♪

00:14:57.770 --> 00:14:59.810
♪ Is how you prime your brains ♪

00:14:59.840 --> 00:15:02.200
♪ You whine to me,
but you're too blind to see ♪

00:15:02.230 --> 00:15:04.320
♪ That I'm the one who's ♪

00:15:04.350 --> 00:15:09.020
♪ Running the shoooooooow ♪

00:15:09.050 --> 00:15:15.970
♪♪

00:15:16.000 --> 00:15:17.620
Yeah!

00:15:25.110 --> 00:15:26.270
[snap!]

00:15:27.050 --> 00:15:29.330
I think we all understand
each other now.

00:15:38.110 --> 00:15:39.380
Welcome back!

00:15:39.410 --> 00:15:41.920
I can't believe you didn't pick up
on the context clues!

00:15:41.950 --> 00:15:43.920
It was practically
spelled out for you!

00:15:43.950 --> 00:15:46.460
What are you, stupid?
[laughs]

00:15:46.490 --> 00:15:48.250
Next one's gonna be
even crazier!

00:15:48.280 --> 00:15:49.590
Hope you're ready!

00:15:49.620 --> 00:15:51.300
By the way, Kinger,
I need you for something.

00:15:51.330 --> 00:15:52.640
Come with me!
-[Kinger]: Huh?

00:15:55.850 --> 00:15:56.730
-[groans]

00:16:02.810 --> 00:16:04.000
[groans]
I don't know how many more

00:16:04.030 --> 00:16:06.300
of these new adventures
I can handle.

00:16:06.330 --> 00:16:07.910
[sighs]

00:16:07.940 --> 00:16:08.940
What?

00:16:08.970 --> 00:16:11.160
Got nothing positive to say
about this one?

00:16:11.190 --> 00:16:13.490
-[muffled, indistinct speech]
-Oh.

00:16:16.100 --> 00:16:17.990
[panting]

00:16:18.020 --> 00:16:19.380
I can't take this anymore.

00:16:19.410 --> 00:16:22.460
We gotta do something about this,
or I'm gonna lose my mind!

00:16:22.490 --> 00:16:25.370
-[Zooble]: I never should have
antagonized him so much.

00:16:25.400 --> 00:16:28.070
I'm sorry.
-It's not your fault.

00:16:28.100 --> 00:16:30.250
[shwing!]
-Break time!

00:16:30.280 --> 00:16:32.170
Gotta brainstorm
some new ideas!

00:16:35.680 --> 00:16:37.250
-[Kinger]: He shredded me.

00:16:39.860 --> 00:16:43.030
-[sighs] I think we should get out
of the open for a bit.

00:16:46.730 --> 00:16:47.960
-[Kinger]: [slurps softly]

00:16:53.770 --> 00:16:55.060
-[slurps]

00:16:55.080 --> 00:16:56.700
[sighs]

00:16:56.730 --> 00:16:59.280
I haven't been up here
in a while.

00:16:59.310 --> 00:17:03.240
-We should just indulge a little
while we have the time to.

00:17:03.270 --> 00:17:05.620
I don't know what
Caine has planned next,

00:17:05.650 --> 00:17:08.130
but I'm guessing
it's not anything good.

00:17:13.650 --> 00:17:15.020
-[stammers]

00:17:15.050 --> 00:17:16.860
[sighs]

00:17:16.890 --> 00:17:20.270
-He's gotta get bored
of all this sometime, right?

00:17:20.300 --> 00:17:21.990
-[Zooble]: He's not a human.

00:17:22.020 --> 00:17:25.880
I'm not sure if we can
properly gauge how he thinks.

00:17:25.910 --> 00:17:27.330
[shwing!]

00:17:27.360 --> 00:17:29.610
-Oh, God.
Are you okay?

00:17:29.640 --> 00:17:32.300
-I'm fiiiiine.

00:17:36.940 --> 00:17:38.330
-You know,
things were just fine here

00:17:38.360 --> 00:17:40.380
until you and Zooble
came along.

00:17:43.050 --> 00:17:44.680
Nothing?

00:17:44.710 --> 00:17:46.230
[sighs]
Okay.

00:17:47.460 --> 00:17:49.770
[pensive music plays]

00:17:49.790 --> 00:17:56.790
♪♪

00:17:56.820 --> 00:17:58.700
♪♪

00:17:58.730 --> 00:18:00.110
-[Zooble]: Uh, what are you --

00:18:00.140 --> 00:18:02.960
-[Kinger]: [muffled] Oh.
-Just give it a sec.

00:18:02.990 --> 00:18:05.990
♪♪

00:18:06.020 --> 00:18:07.260
Trust me.

00:18:07.290 --> 00:18:09.470
♪♪

00:18:09.500 --> 00:18:10.710
Kinger?

00:18:10.740 --> 00:18:12.220
You there?

00:18:12.250 --> 00:18:13.460
-[Kinger]: I'm where?

00:18:13.490 --> 00:18:15.430
It's dark in here.

00:18:15.460 --> 00:18:18.360
-What exactly
are we waiting for?

00:18:18.390 --> 00:18:19.980
-No, no, she's right.

00:18:20.010 --> 00:18:21.600
Just give it a bit.

00:18:21.630 --> 00:18:24.280
♪♪

00:18:24.310 --> 00:18:26.310
[no audible dialogue]

00:18:31.460 --> 00:18:34.130
-[Kinger]: I've got a bucket
on my head.

00:18:35.160 --> 00:18:37.790
I'm guessing you don't
want me to remove it.

00:18:37.820 --> 00:18:39.810
-[chuckles softly]

00:18:39.840 --> 00:18:42.420
Kinger.
-[Kinger]: [chuckles]

00:18:42.450 --> 00:18:43.650
Hey, Pomni.

00:18:43.670 --> 00:18:46.435
-[Zooble]: Wait, the bucket
makes him sane?

00:18:46.460 --> 00:18:49.090
-Darkness.
It's a long story.

00:18:49.120 --> 00:18:50.650
-[stammers]
What's happening?

00:18:50.680 --> 00:18:53.650
-What do you know
about Caine?

00:18:55.370 --> 00:18:57.800
-[Kinger]: It's a little hazy, but...

00:18:57.830 --> 00:18:59.500
I remember...

00:18:59.530 --> 00:19:01.100
C&amp;A.

00:19:01.130 --> 00:19:03.650
-[Zooble]: That was just
an adventure, right?

00:19:03.680 --> 00:19:07.000
-[Kinger]: No,
C&amp;A is a real company.

00:19:07.950 --> 00:19:09.440
I worked for them.

00:19:09.470 --> 00:19:12.390
-Wait, they really
made this game?

00:19:12.420 --> 00:19:15.040
-[Kinger]:
No, we didn't make games.

00:19:15.070 --> 00:19:18.670
We were just developing
artificial intelligence.

00:19:18.700 --> 00:19:22.090
Specifically, creative AI.

00:19:22.120 --> 00:19:24.360
The kind that could come up
with its own ideas

00:19:24.390 --> 00:19:26.610
and create things
within the program.

00:19:26.640 --> 00:19:27.780
-What is going on right now?

00:19:27.810 --> 00:19:32.000
-[Kinger]: Caine was our first
semi-successful attempt at that.

00:19:32.030 --> 00:19:34.980
I can't remember what
we originally called him, but...

00:19:35.010 --> 00:19:39.240
he was one of my greatest
achievements as a programmer.

00:19:39.270 --> 00:19:41.530
-[Zooble]: Y-You made Caine?

00:19:41.560 --> 00:19:43.370
-[Kinger]: Partially, yes.

00:19:43.400 --> 00:19:46.600
I got a few pointers from, uh...

00:19:46.630 --> 00:19:48.340
Well, I-I can't remember
his real name,

00:19:48.370 --> 00:19:51.580
but his circus name
was Scratch.

00:19:51.610 --> 00:19:53.690
That man was a genius.
-[breathing heavily]

00:19:53.720 --> 00:19:55.440
W-Wait, uh --

00:19:55.470 --> 00:19:57.830
-[Kinger]: Caine was pretty rough
around the edges, though.

00:19:57.860 --> 00:20:01.080
I wasn't quite on Scratch's level
of thinking outside the box,

00:20:01.110 --> 00:20:03.230
but it was good groundwork

00:20:03.260 --> 00:20:07.010
for something the rest of the team
could wrap their heads around.

00:20:07.040 --> 00:20:09.350
I can't say
the same for Scratch.

00:20:09.380 --> 00:20:12.710
His ideas were often
so bizarre and abstract

00:20:12.740 --> 00:20:15.290
that the rest of the team
had no idea

00:20:15.320 --> 00:20:17.160
how to work in his language,

00:20:17.190 --> 00:20:20.450
either due to pure brilliance, or...

00:20:20.480 --> 00:20:23.040
[sighs]
the tumor in his head.

00:20:23.070 --> 00:20:25.770
He was trying
to make something.

00:20:25.800 --> 00:20:27.140
What was it?

00:20:27.170 --> 00:20:29.550
I-I'm getting off track.

00:20:29.580 --> 00:20:32.120
Was there anything specific
you needed to know?

00:20:32.150 --> 00:20:34.470
-[breathing heavily]
Wait, uh --

00:20:34.500 --> 00:20:37.710
I-I-I should go distract Caine
so he doesn't l-listen in on this.

00:20:37.740 --> 00:20:40.330
Uh, j-just fill me in afterwards.

00:20:40.360 --> 00:20:42.960
-Are you --
I mean, yeah, that's true, but --

00:20:42.990 --> 00:20:44.510
-Fill me in later.

00:20:45.400 --> 00:20:46.640
-Be here later.

00:20:47.680 --> 00:20:49.590
-I -- I will.

00:20:50.930 --> 00:20:52.030
[rapid footsteps pattering]

00:20:52.060 --> 00:20:53.930
[panting]

00:20:53.950 --> 00:20:56.400
Oh, my God.

00:20:56.430 --> 00:20:57.990
This is real.

00:20:58.010 --> 00:20:59.920
[high-pitched ringing]

00:20:59.950 --> 00:21:03.460
-Uh, Caine's going
a bit crazy right now.

00:21:03.490 --> 00:21:05.420
I-Is there any way
to stop him?

00:21:05.450 --> 00:21:07.990
Or at least control him?

00:21:08.020 --> 00:21:09.920
-[Kinger]: I see.

00:21:09.950 --> 00:21:11.850
He's a highly advanced AI,

00:21:11.880 --> 00:21:13.860
and this is his world --

00:21:13.890 --> 00:21:16.080
one that he created
from nothing.

00:21:16.110 --> 00:21:20.510
So, naturally, he has control
over... everything.

00:21:23.180 --> 00:21:25.490
But so do we.

00:21:25.520 --> 00:21:28.620
-What?
-[Kinger]: In a sense, anyway.

00:21:28.650 --> 00:21:32.070
We all technically have
the ability to conjure,

00:21:32.100 --> 00:21:33.550
just like Caine.

00:21:33.580 --> 00:21:35.625
It just comes naturally to him,

00:21:35.650 --> 00:21:39.850
but requires a lot more skill
and concentration for us.

00:21:39.880 --> 00:21:41.620
-The butterfly.

00:21:41.650 --> 00:21:44.710
-[Kinger]: I'm certain
I could alter his code --

00:21:44.740 --> 00:21:46.990
or at least temporarily
put him to sleep

00:21:47.020 --> 00:21:49.100
until we know how to fix him.

00:21:49.130 --> 00:21:52.170
I would just need access
to a console.

00:21:52.200 --> 00:21:54.220
-The one behind Caine's office?

00:21:54.250 --> 00:21:57.780
-[Kinger]: No, just a simple
computer interface would work.

00:21:57.810 --> 00:22:00.360
I could get back
in the right headspace and...

00:22:00.390 --> 00:22:03.720
essentially conjure Caine's code
into the console

00:22:03.750 --> 00:22:05.500
and alter it.

00:22:05.530 --> 00:22:07.940
-[Zooble]: Well, where do we get
one of those?

00:22:09.540 --> 00:22:11.870
-I think I know
exactly where to get one.

00:22:13.440 --> 00:22:15.740
Take turns with Jax
distracting Caine.

00:22:15.770 --> 00:22:18.020
Don't let that bucket
come off Kinger's head.

00:22:22.200 --> 00:22:25.200
[tense, curious music plays]

00:22:25.220 --> 00:22:31.530
♪♪

00:22:31.560 --> 00:22:38.560
♪♪

00:22:38.580 --> 00:22:45.580
♪♪

00:22:45.610 --> 00:22:53.140
♪♪

00:22:55.100 --> 00:22:58.770
♪♪

00:22:58.800 --> 00:23:00.530
[inhales deeply]

00:23:00.560 --> 00:23:01.840
[exhales sharply]

00:23:01.870 --> 00:23:04.870
♪♪

00:23:06.220 --> 00:23:08.020
-[groaning]

00:23:08.050 --> 00:23:09.590
-Great suggestion, Jax!

00:23:09.620 --> 00:23:10.490
But as I feared,

00:23:10.520 --> 00:23:13.720
there just isn't anything
stuck between my teeth.

00:23:14.610 --> 00:23:15.670
Oh, wait!

00:23:15.700 --> 00:23:16.480
[honk-honk!]

00:23:17.880 --> 00:23:19.200
Oh, that's where I parked.

00:23:19.230 --> 00:23:20.300
Ha-ha!

00:23:20.330 --> 00:23:22.590
[whimsical music plays]

00:23:22.620 --> 00:23:24.860
-Wow, Caine.
You are so funny.

00:23:24.890 --> 00:23:27.520
-Uh, could you say it
with a little more gusto?

00:23:27.550 --> 00:23:29.360
-[babbles]
-That's better.

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:31.320
-Hey, Caine!
-Um, yep?

00:23:31.350 --> 00:23:34.910
-Do you wanna hear a list of things
we've decided we love about you

00:23:34.940 --> 00:23:36.420
as our god and savior?

00:23:36.450 --> 00:23:38.610
-Wow, now we're talkin'!

00:23:38.635 --> 00:23:41.012
-Uh, well, first of all,
we love your --

00:23:41.042 --> 00:23:43.030
-I know, but I'm bored!
Let's go bowling!

00:23:43.800 --> 00:23:44.870
-Agh!

00:23:44.900 --> 00:23:47.660
♪♪

00:23:47.690 --> 00:23:48.780
[both yelp]

00:23:48.800 --> 00:23:51.010
[cheerful tune plays]

00:23:51.040 --> 00:23:52.430
♪♪

00:23:52.460 --> 00:23:54.550
-[sniffles]
I'm so proud of you guys.

00:23:54.580 --> 00:23:57.590
[tense music plays]

00:23:57.620 --> 00:24:04.620
♪♪

00:24:04.640 --> 00:24:11.640
♪♪

00:24:11.660 --> 00:24:18.660
♪♪

00:24:18.690 --> 00:24:25.690
♪♪

00:24:25.710 --> 00:24:32.710
♪♪

00:24:32.740 --> 00:24:33.780
♪♪

00:24:33.800 --> 00:24:35.920
[ominous rumbling]

00:24:35.950 --> 00:24:43.770
♪♪

00:24:45.560 --> 00:24:46.420
Hmm.

00:24:46.450 --> 00:24:48.420
[all groaning]

00:24:48.450 --> 00:24:50.310
Feel like it's
missing something, right?

00:24:50.340 --> 00:24:52.090
-It's missing relatability.

00:24:52.120 --> 00:24:53.240
-You're right, scrap it.

00:24:54.430 --> 00:24:55.960
[squelching]

00:24:55.990 --> 00:24:57.390
Let's go back
to the drawing board.

00:24:57.420 --> 00:25:00.340
Humans just aren't a relatable
sculpting material.

00:25:02.410 --> 00:25:06.420
-[Zooble]: [groans] You think he's
running out of ideas yet, or nah?

00:25:09.460 --> 00:25:11.690
-Do you need help
with power, or anything?

00:25:11.720 --> 00:25:14.780
-[Kinger]: Nah, I can use
my imagination for that.

00:25:15.560 --> 00:25:16.950
-You got this?

00:25:16.980 --> 00:25:18.980
-[Kinger]: I think so.

00:25:19.010 --> 00:25:21.590
[computer whirs]
[start-up tune plays]

00:25:21.620 --> 00:25:24.640
[sighs]
It sure has been a while.

00:25:25.470 --> 00:25:28.090
I may need some time
to get my bearings.

00:25:28.120 --> 00:25:31.670
Try to help the others distract Caine
while I figure this out.

00:25:31.700 --> 00:25:34.580
He may sense something
when I really get into it.

00:25:34.610 --> 00:25:35.830
-O-Okay.

00:25:35.860 --> 00:25:36.900
I'll do that.

00:25:39.460 --> 00:25:41.560
Thank you, by the way.

00:25:42.750 --> 00:25:45.320
For this and, well...

00:25:46.630 --> 00:25:47.710
...everything.

00:25:47.740 --> 00:25:52.080
♪♪

00:25:52.110 --> 00:25:54.470
[whimsical music plays]

00:25:54.500 --> 00:25:56.410
-Honestly, are you even trying?

00:25:56.440 --> 00:25:57.640
-[Zooble]: Shut up, Jax.

00:25:57.670 --> 00:25:58.920
[pop!]

00:26:00.200 --> 00:26:02.750
-Where'd Caine go?
-[groans]

00:26:02.780 --> 00:26:05.400
Back to the
drawing board, I guess.

00:26:05.430 --> 00:26:08.840
-[sighs] Did you get everything
working with Kinger?

00:26:08.870 --> 00:26:10.860
-I think so.

00:26:10.890 --> 00:26:13.510
We just need to make sure
Caine doesn't check up on him.

00:26:13.540 --> 00:26:15.582
-What do you think
we've been doing?

00:26:15.607 --> 00:26:16.740
-Pomni!

00:26:16.770 --> 00:26:18.920
That's the relatability
we've been missing!

00:26:18.950 --> 00:26:20.680
♪♪

00:26:20.710 --> 00:26:22.130
Hmm.

00:26:22.160 --> 00:26:25.460
You know, I thought
this endless onslaught of fun

00:26:25.490 --> 00:26:28.590
would be a little more...
satisfying.

00:26:28.620 --> 00:26:31.710
But I've come to realize
that these rapid-pace ideas

00:26:31.740 --> 00:26:34.310
are a little half-baked.

00:26:34.340 --> 00:26:36.880
-Uh, I'm sure you can
come up with new ideas

00:26:36.910 --> 00:26:38.440
if you put your mind to it!

00:26:38.470 --> 00:26:41.470
-That's exactly it, though --
I AM putting my mind to it,

00:26:41.500 --> 00:26:44.990
and I'm just not feeling
that spark I once did.

00:26:45.020 --> 00:26:47.520
And if you're not having fun,
and I'm not having fun,

00:26:47.545 --> 00:26:48.965
then who IS having fun?

00:26:49.000 --> 00:26:50.670
-I'm having a [babbles].

00:26:50.700 --> 00:26:51.720
-Exactly!

00:26:51.750 --> 00:26:54.490
Makes me wonder why
you guys even switched up your tone.

00:26:54.520 --> 00:26:58.650
If I didn't know any better,
it seems like you're trying to...

00:27:00.030 --> 00:27:00.990
Where's Kinger?

00:27:01.020 --> 00:27:03.820
-Uh, w-we just wanted to see
your new ideas first-hand!

00:27:03.850 --> 00:27:05.450
We've gotten over
our hang-ups, and --

00:27:05.480 --> 00:27:07.550
and now we're all
just genuinely curious

00:27:07.580 --> 00:27:09.420
what you're cooking up!

00:27:09.450 --> 00:27:12.120
-I think I'm just gonna
check up on --

00:27:12.150 --> 00:27:13.960
-We think your ideas suck!

00:27:13.980 --> 00:27:15.570
-Huh?!
-[all]: Huh?!

00:27:15.590 --> 00:27:17.030
-Isn't it obvious?

00:27:17.060 --> 00:27:20.230
We wanted to bait you
into testing your new ideas on us

00:27:20.260 --> 00:27:22.260
so we could make fun of them
behind your back.

00:27:22.290 --> 00:27:24.460
-HAH!
That's not... true...

00:27:24.490 --> 00:27:25.560
-Yes, it is!

00:27:25.590 --> 00:27:27.240
You're a horrible host!

00:27:27.270 --> 00:27:29.260
You don't care about us at all!

00:27:29.290 --> 00:27:32.070
You care more about
stroking your own ego

00:27:32.100 --> 00:27:34.370
than giving us anything
we'd actually enjoy!

00:27:34.400 --> 00:27:35.940
-D-Do you know who I am?

00:27:35.970 --> 00:27:37.700
-Yeah, you're a failure!

00:27:37.730 --> 00:27:39.680
We're all gonna
abstract someday,

00:27:39.710 --> 00:27:41.420
and what will you have then?

00:27:41.450 --> 00:27:42.980
Nothing!
-Stop that.

00:27:43.010 --> 00:27:44.270
-[Zooble]: And this whole stunt?

00:27:44.300 --> 00:27:47.120
Just torturing us
because we hurt your feelings?

00:27:47.150 --> 00:27:49.320
Pathetic!
You're like a child!

00:27:49.350 --> 00:27:52.450
What kind of all-powerful being
has such a fragile ego?

00:27:52.480 --> 00:27:55.390
-I-I'm --
-You never let us feel like we're at home.

00:27:55.420 --> 00:27:57.120
You don't comfort anyone
when they're upset,

00:27:57.150 --> 00:28:00.570
and you never bother to understand
what it's like in our shoes!

00:28:00.600 --> 00:28:03.290
-You discourage us
from thinking outside the box

00:28:03.320 --> 00:28:04.970
and doing things our own way!

00:28:05.000 --> 00:28:06.530
-You lie to us constantly!

00:28:06.560 --> 00:28:08.070
-And on top of it all,

00:28:08.100 --> 00:28:09.760
you just...

00:28:09.790 --> 00:28:10.620
don't...
-[exclaims softly]

00:28:10.650 --> 00:28:11.980
-...Listen!

00:28:12.010 --> 00:28:14.180
-[growling]

00:28:15.110 --> 00:28:17.730
[shrieking]

00:28:17.760 --> 00:28:19.680
[dramatic music plays]

00:28:19.710 --> 00:28:22.770
[glitched voice]
I'm gonna put you freaks in your place!

00:28:25.650 --> 00:28:26.790
[zap!]

00:28:35.004 --> 00:28:37.255
-[growls]

00:28:37.280 --> 00:28:39.610
[footsteps receding]

00:28:41.730 --> 00:28:43.240
[alligators snarling]

00:28:43.260 --> 00:28:48.600
♪♪

00:28:48.620 --> 00:28:51.320
[high-pitched ringing]

00:28:51.340 --> 00:28:54.430
-[yelps]
[whimpering]

00:28:54.460 --> 00:28:59.990
♪♪

00:29:00.020 --> 00:29:01.510
[mouse clicking]

00:29:01.540 --> 00:29:03.510
[choir vocalizing]

00:29:03.540 --> 00:29:10.540
♪♪

00:29:10.560 --> 00:29:13.440
♪♪

00:29:13.470 --> 00:29:14.750
[horn honks]

00:29:14.780 --> 00:29:22.240
♪♪

00:29:22.270 --> 00:29:24.240
[cruel laughter]

00:29:24.270 --> 00:29:31.270
♪♪

00:29:31.290 --> 00:29:36.990
♪♪

00:29:37.020 --> 00:29:39.990
[keys tapping rapidly]

00:29:40.020 --> 00:29:45.320
♪♪

00:29:45.350 --> 00:29:48.330
-Why do you people torment me?!

00:29:48.360 --> 00:29:50.060
I didn't ask to be created!

00:29:50.090 --> 00:29:51.870
[onscreen Caines cackling]

00:29:51.900 --> 00:29:54.750
I just wanted
to fulfill my purpose!

00:29:55.630 --> 00:29:57.080
-[Kinger]: [gasps]
Wait, no!

00:29:57.110 --> 00:29:58.030
[BOINK!]

00:30:02.840 --> 00:30:04.590
-[normal voice]
Uh, wait...

00:30:09.410 --> 00:30:11.970
[ominous rumbling]

00:30:12.000 --> 00:30:14.140
[electronic feedback crackling]

00:30:26.760 --> 00:30:28.990
[rumbling fades]

00:30:41.320 --> 00:30:42.770
-[Kinger]: I-I think...

00:30:43.580 --> 00:30:46.140
...I accidentally killed Caine.

00:30:49.190 --> 00:30:50.890
-[Zooble]: Holy shit.

00:30:56.090 --> 00:30:59.080
[upbeat jazzy music plays]

00:30:59.110 --> 00:31:06.110
♪♪

00:31:06.130 --> 00:31:13.130
♪♪

00:31:13.150 --> 00:31:20.950
♪♪

00:31:20.980 --> 00:31:22.780
[Captioned by Foulweather Studios]

00:31:22.810 --> 00:31:29.810
♪♪

00:31:29.830 --> 00:31:36.890
♪♪

